## SECTION 1: PROJECT OVERVIEW
====================================

**Project Name:** Smoke-Free Tracker

**Problem Statement:**
Quitting smoking is incredibly challenging due to physical addiction (nicotine) and psychological dependence (habits/triggers). Smokers often relapse because they lack visible proof of their progress, feel isolated without a support system, and fail to realize the immediate financial and health benefits of quitting. 

**Why this project was created:**
To provide a comprehensive, encouraging, and data-driven companion for individuals trying to quit smoking. Visualizing success (like money saved or hours of life regained) is a powerful psychological motivator.

**Real-world use case:**
A person deciding to quit smoking registers on the app. Every time they have a craving, instead of smoking, they open the app, log the craving, read community posts, and look at the health milestones they've unlocked (like "Carbon Monoxide levels back to normal"). This replaces the habit of smoking with a positive reinforcement habit.

**Target users:**
Individuals actively trying to quit smoking, those thinking about quitting, or people who have recently quit and want to maintain their streak.

**Business value:**
Can be monetized via premium features (advanced analytics, one-on-one coaching, NRT (Nicotine Replacement Therapy) product partnerships), or adopted by health insurance companies/clinics as a patient monitoring tool.

**Key features:**
1. Live Quit Time Counter (Days, Hours, Minutes, Seconds)
2. Dynamic Health Timeline based on actual time elapsed
3. Achievements and Badge system for motivation
4. Cravings Tracker with graphical analytics (Chart.js)
5. Overall Progress stats (Cigarettes Avoided, Money Saved, Time Won Back)
6. Community Feed for peer support
7. Support & Helplines quick access
8. Progressive Web App (PWA) allowing offline access and native app installation.

*Interview Explanation:* "My project is 'Smoke-Free Tracker', a Progressive Web App designed to help people quit smoking. It solves the problem of relapse by providing real-time visual progress—like exact money saved and health milestones reached. I built it using a Spring Boot backend and a vanilla JavaScript PWA frontend to ensure it's lightning-fast and works offline. It features a community feed, cravings analytics, and automated achievement unlocks."

